:: Eden Halloween
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cabin">><<effects>><<wearProp "halloween">>
<<speechresolve>>
Orange autumn leaves decorate the trees of the forest, covering the ground and crunching under your feet as you approach Eden, the hamper of sweets in your hands. <<He>> momentarily looks up from <<his>> work to regard you, but stops when <<he>> notices what you're holding.
<br><br>

<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek" "shy">>
		"H-Happy Halloween," you say, holding the hamper out to <<him>> with both hands.
	<<case "polite">>
		"Happy Halloween," you say warmly, offering the hamper to <<him>>.
	<<case "docile">>
		"Happy Halloween," you say, carefully presenting the hamper to <<him>>.
	<<case "flamboyant">>
		"Happy Halloween, darling," you say, offering the hamper with a bright smile.
	<<case "bratty">>
		"Happy Halloween," you say, nudging the hamper into <<his>> hands.
	<<case "cruel">>
		"Happy Halloween," you say, pressing the hamper at <<him>> like a challenge.
	<<case "confident">>
		"Happy Halloween," you say, handing the hamper over like you knew <<he>> would take it.
	<<case "special">>
		"Happy Halloween," you say, offering the hamper with a look that dares <<him>> to refuse it.
	<<default>>
		"Happy Halloween," you say, passing the hamper to <<him>>.
<</switch>>
<br><br>

"Sweets?" <<he>> asks, looking your gift over. "This is unexpected."
<br><br>

<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek" "shy">>
		"Well, s-since you don't trick-or-treat, I thought I could bring the sweets to you," you say.
	<<case "polite">>
		"Since you don't go trick-or-treating, I thought you might appreciate some sweets anyway," you say.
	<<case "docile">>
		"You don't go trick-or-treating, so I thought I should bring something to you instead," you say.
	<<case "flamboyant">>
		"Since you won't go trick-or-treating, I thought I'd bring the sweets to you instead," you say lightly.
	<<case "bratty">>
		"Even if you don't go trick-or-treating, there's no reason not to have sweets," you say.
	<<case "cruel">>
		"If you insist on staying out here instead of trick-or-treating, you can at least have sweets," you say.
	<<case "confident">>
		"You don't go trick-or-treating, so I figured I'd bring Halloween to you," you say.
	<<case "special">>
		"You weren't going to go out for sweets yourself, so I brought them to you," you say.
	<<default>>
		"I just thought you'd appreciate it since you don't go trick or treating," you say.
<</switch>>
<br><br>

Eden glances at the hamper again, an unsure but grateful look in <<his>> eyes. "Thanks," <<he>> says. "It's nice, not that I eat a lot of sweets anyway."
As <<he>> starts toward the kitchen to store the hamper away, your eyes catch on the dining table instead. A knife rests beside a few pumpkins, their vivid orange skin standing out against the muted wood and the autumn light filtering through the cabin.
<br><br>

Eden notices your gaze and stops, placing the hamper down. "I was planning on making pumpkin pie," <<he>> says, eyeing the spread on the table.
<br><br>

<<link [[Ask to carve pumpkins|Eden Carve]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Nod|Eden Nod]]>><</link>>

:: Eden Nod
<<effects>>

You nod your head in response. Eden opens a nearby cabinet to store the sweets away, but suddenly changes <<his>> mind and looks to you.
<br><br>

"Why don't you share these with me," <<he>> asks.
<br><br>

<<link [[Accept|Eden Sweets]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Refuse|Eden Sweets Refuse]]>><</link>>

:: Eden Sweets Refuse
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>

You shake your head.

<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek" "shy">>
		"I-I bought these sweets for you."
	<<case "polite">>
		"They're for you. I bought them with you in mind."
	<<case "docile">>
		"I bought them for you... You should keep them."
	<<case "flamboyant">>
		"No, no, they're yours. I brought them for you."
	<<case "bratty">>
		"I got these sweets for you. It's yours."
	<<case "cruel">>
		"I brought them for you, so stop trying to hand them back."
	<<case "confident">>
		"I brought them for you, not for me."
	<<case "special">>
		"They're yours. I didn't come all this way just to keep them for myself."
	<<default>>
		"I bought the sweets for you."
<</switch>>
<br><br>

Eden shrugs and stores the hamper in the cabinet. <<He>> goes over to you and kisses your forehead. "Thanks again," <<he>> says, before walking away.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Eden Cabin]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Eden Carve
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>

"Can we carve pumpkins?" you ask.
<br><br>

"What?" <<he>> questions, pulling an incredulous expression. "I was saving these for pie, not carving."
<br><br>

<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek" "shy">>
		"Please?" you say.
	<<case "polite">>
		"Please? It would make the cabin feel festive," you say.
	<<case "docile">>
		"Please. Just two?" you ask hopefully.
	<<case "flamboyant">>
		"Please? It's Halloween," you say, dragging the words out playfully.
	<<case "bratty">>
		"Oh, come on, it's Halloween!" you say.
	<<case "cruel">>
		"You can spare two pumpkins for carving," you say. "You'll live."
	<<case "confident">>
		"It's Halloween. We should carve them," you say.
	<<case "special">>
		"It's Halloween. Don't tell me you're too serious for pumpkins," you say.
	<<default>>
		"But it's Halloween," you say.
<</switch>>
<br><br>

Eden sighs and looks away, considering for a moment, before looking back to you. "Fine," <<he>> says. "But we're only using two of them."
<br><br>

A smile spreads across your face before you can stop it, and you hurry over to the table.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Eden Carve 2]]>><<pass 20>><</link>>

:: Eden Carve 2
<<effects>><<wearProp "knife">>

Grabbing a knife, you and Eden sit at opposite ends of the dining table. You decide to carve
<br><br>

<<link [[Something scary|Eden Carve 3]]>><<set $phase to 0>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Something cute|Eden Carve 3]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Eden|Eden Carve 3]]>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>

:: Eden Carve 3
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>

Using your knife, you whittle away at the surface of the pumpkin.

<<if currentSkillValue('tending') gte 150>>
	<<if $phase is 0>>
		It takes a while, but the finishing result looks rather scary.
	<<elseif $phase is 1>>
		It takes a while, but the finishing result looks rather cute.
	<<elseif $phase is 2>>
		It takes a while, but the finishing result looks relatively similar to Eden.
	<</if>>
<<else>>

	<<if $phase is 0>>
		You try your best, but the carving doesn't look very scary.
	<<elseif $phase is 1>>
		You try your best, but the carving doesn't look very cute.
	<<elseif $phase is 2>>
		You try your best, but the carving doesn't look very similar to Eden.
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

Stepping back from your work, you walk over to Eden to look at <<his>> creation. <<He>> has carved the image of a deer into the pumpkin. It looks skilfully done, the sort of patient work that makes it obvious how practiced <<he>> is with <<his>> hands.
<br><br>

<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek" "shy">>
		"Y-your pumpkin looks cute," you say.
	<<case "polite">>
		"Your pumpkin turned out really cute," you say.
	<<case "docile">>
		"It looks cute," you say softly, admiring the carving.
	<<case "flamboyant">>
		"Your pumpkin is adorable," you say with a grin.
	<<case "bratty">>
		"That's a cute pumpkin," you say.
	<<case "cruel">>
		"For something you were so grumpy about, that turned out cute," you say.
	<<case "confident">>
		"That's a cute carving," you say. "You did well."
	<<case "special">>
		"Your pumpkin's cute," you say. "Almost annoyingly so."
	<<default>>
		"That pumpkin looks cute," you say.
<</switch>>
<br><br>

Eden turns <<his>> head to face you. "If pumpkins are cute, maybe I should start calling you pumpkin too," <<he>> laughs, playfully smacking your ass.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Eden Carve 4]]>><</link>>

:: Eden Carve 4
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>

After a while, Eden drops <<his>> knife and walks over to you, evaluating your carving.
<br><br>

<<if currentSkillValue('tending') gte 150>>
	<<if $phase is 0>>
		"Wow, that's scary," <<he>> says. <<He>> looks impressed.
	<<elseif $phase is 1>>
		"Wow, that's cute," <<he>> says. <<He>> looks impressed.
	<<elseif $phase is 2>>
		<<He>> drinks in your work with a look of slight surprise on <<his>> face, almost unbelieving of what <<he>> sees.
		"Is that me?" <<he>> asks, turning <<his>> head to you.
		<br><br>

		<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
			<<case "meek" "shy">>
				You nod your head.
			<<case "polite">>
				"Yes," you say with a small smile.
			<<case "docile">>
				"Yes," you murmur.
			<<case "flamboyant">>
				"Of course," you say brightly.
			<<case "bratty">>
				"Yeah," you say.
			<<case "cruel">>
				"Obviously," you say.
			<<case "confident">>
				"Yes. It is," you say.
			<<case "special">>
				"Maybe," you say, then smile. "Yes."
			<<default>>
				"Yes," you say.
		<</switch>>
		<br><br>

		"That's good," <<he>> says, nodding slightly.
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<He>> stares at it for a bit, trying to discern what it's supposed to be.
	<br>

	<<if $phase is 0>>
		"It's supposed to be scary," you say.
	<<elseif $phase is 1>>
		"It's supposed to be cute," you say.
	<<elseif $phase is 2>>
		"It's supposed to be you," you say.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	Eden shoots you a smirk, clearly trying not to laugh too hard. "It's a good effort," <<he>> says, patting you on the head.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Eden Carve 5]]>><</link>>

:: Eden Carve 5
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>

After a short deliberation, the two of you decide to decorate the cabin with your work. Eden opens the wooden door, and a wash of cool autumn air brushes across your face and slips beneath your clothes.
<<He>> places the pumpkins near the entrance. Their carved faces lend the severe little cabin a soft festive touch it normally lacks.
<br><br>

When you're done admiring your work, you and Eden walk back inside. Looking to the table again, your eyes are drawn to the hamper of sweets.
<br><br>

<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek" "shy">>
		"Y-you haven't eaten the sweets yet," you say.
	<<case "polite">>
		"You still haven't tried the sweets yet," you say.
	<<case "docile">>
		"You haven't had any yet," you point out softly.
	<<case "flamboyant">>
		"You still haven't tried the sweets," you say, eyeing the hamper.
	<<case "bratty">>
		"Hey, you still haven't tried the sweets yet," you say.
	<<case "cruel">>
		"You still haven't touched the sweets I brought," you say.
	<<case "confident">>
		"You still haven't tried them," you say, nodding toward the hamper.
	<<case "special">>
		"You haven't even tasted them yet," you say.
	<<default>>
		"You haven't tried the sweets yet," you say.
<</switch>>
<br><br>

Eden looks to the table, seemingly contemplating something. "Why don't you share them with me?" <<he>> asks.
<br><br>

<<link [[Accept|Eden Sweets]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Refuse|Eden Sweets Refuse]]>><</link>>

:: Eden Sweets
<<effects>>

You accept Eden's offer and walk to the table. Grabbing one of the knives, <<he>> cuts open the hamper's protective plastic and reaches for a small box tucked within its centre.
<br><br>

Upon opening the box, you both find it filled with creamy chocolate. The rich scent rises at once, thick and sweet enough to make your mouth water.
<br><br>

Taking a piece, Eden brings it to <<his>> mouth.
<br><br>

<<link [[Snatch it from Eden|Eden Sweets 2]]>><<set $phase2 to 1>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Let Eden eat it|Eden Sweets 2]]>><</link>>

:: Eden Sweets 2
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>

<<if $phase2 is 1>>
	<<wearProp "chocolate">><<canvas-model-override "mouth" "chew">>
	Just before the chocolate enters <<his>> mouth, you snatch it from Eden and gobble it up.
	<br><br>

	"Hey!" Eden exclaims, turning to you.
	<br><br>
	<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
		<<case "meek" "shy">>
			"Y-you told me we were sharing," you tease.
		<<case "polite">>
			"You did say we were sharing," you remind <<him>>, teasingly.
		<<case "docile">>
			"You said we were sharing," you say with a small smile.
		<<case "flamboyant">>
			"You said we were sharing," you tease. "I'm only taking you seriously."
		<<case "bratty">>
			"What? You did tell me we were sharing," you tease.
		<<case "cruel">>
			"You said we were sharing. Don't complain now," you tease.
		<<case "confident">>
			"You said we were sharing," you say, looking pleased with yourself.
		<<case "special">>
			"You offered to share," you tease. "I'm just participating."
		<<default>>
			"You told me we were sharing," you tease.
	<</switch>>
	<br><br>

	Eden opens <<his>> mouth to retort, but stops. <<His>> eyes glint and a mischievous smirk spreads across <<his>> face. "Okay. We're sharing," <<he>> says, slowly and tantalisingly swiping <<his>> finger over one of the chocolates.
	<br><br>

	<<He>> brings <<his>> chocolate-coated finger up to your mouth, looking at you with heated eyes. "Come on. I know you want to."
<<else>>
	You watch Eden eat the piece of chocolate. <<He>> seems to enjoy its sweetness.
	<br><br>

	"Haven't eaten chocolate in a while," <<he>> says. Turning to you, <<he>> offers you the box. "Want one?"
	<br><br>

	You're about to reply, before Eden perks up. <<His>> eyes glint and a mischievous smirk spreads across <<his>> face. "I think I can make this more interesting," <<he>> says, slowly and tantalisingly swiping <<his>> finger over one of the chocolates.
	<br><br>

	<<He>> brings <<his>> chocolate-coated finger up to your mouth, looking at you with heated eyes. "Come on. I know you want to."
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Lick Eden's finger|Eden Sweets Lick]]>><<canvas-model-override "clear">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Refuse|Eden Sweets Lick Refuse]]>><<canvas-model-override "clear">><</link>>

:: Eden Sweets Lick Refuse
<<effects>>

You turn your face away. Eden chuckles at you, before licking the chocolate off <<his>> finger and kissing you on the forehead.
<br><br>

"Thanks for the sweets," <<he>> says. Grabbing the hamper, <<he>> stores it in a nearby cabinet and walks away.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Eden Cabin]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Eden Sweets Lick
<<effects>>

You slowly close your lips around <<his>> finger. With slow strokes of your tongue, you lick and suck the chocolate away while Eden watches you with hungry, unwavering attention.
<br><br>

"Good <<girl>>," <<he>> says, sliding <<his>> finger down your tongue and popping it out of your mouth. <<He>> reaches into the box.
<br><br>

"Since you did so well with that," <<he>> says, selecting another piece and trapping it lightly between <<his>> teeth before tugging you closer.
<br><br>

<<link [[Kiss Eden|Eden Sweets Sex]]>><<set $sexstart to 1>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Pull away|Eden Sweets Pull Away]]>><</link>>

:: Eden Sweets Pull Away
<<effects>>

You pull away from Eden's hold. <<He>> chuckles at you, before finishing the chocolate <<himself>> and kissing you on the forehead.
<br><br>

"Thanks for the sweets," <<he>> says. Grabbing the hamper, <<he>> stores it in a nearby cabinet and walks away.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Eden Cabin]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

